  "mechanismSummary": "Propan-1-ol attacks chlorodimethylsulfonium ion at sulfur, and the proton is lost: an alkoxysulfonium ion. Triethylamine removes a proton from an S-methyl group, giving a sulfonium ylide, which takes the hydrogen on the alcohol carbon through a five-membered ring. The C=O forms and dimethyl sulfide (which smells strongly) leaves. A primary alcohol stops at the aldehyde.",
  "references": [
    "Clayden, Greeves and Warren, Organic Chemistry, 2nd edition (Oxford University Press), chapter 23"
  ],
